-- Strata: the kernel Meadow's two levels are checked by.
--
-- `docs/2LTT.md` is the plan. Meadow gains a compile-time level above the
-- language it is today, a total dependent type theory, and opt-in erased
-- dependent functions at run time; both are checked here. The kernel is
-- Idyll's, shared with Idyll: its core calculus, normalisation by
-- evaluation, unification, termination and dependent matching are here,
-- and staging is to come. The package depends on no front end, so that both
-- front ends can depend on it.
--
-- What it holds: the two levels, and how a definition's level is decided
-- before its body is elaborated (`Level`); and Idyll's kernel, moved here
-- from Idyll's `front/` unchanged but for its module paths: grades
-- (`Grade`), the names and literals the kernel shares with a renamer
-- (`Hir`), terms (`Core`) and values (`Value`), the checker's state (`Tc`)
-- and context (`Ctx`), normalisation by evaluation (`Eval`), unification
-- (`Unify`), termination (`Termination`), strict positivity (`Positivity`),
-- usage (`Usage`), strongly connected components (`Graph`), and the
-- splitting of a variable into its constructors that dependent matching is
-- built on (`Cases`); and a checker of whole Core terms made of these
-- parts, which a front end can run over the Core it elaborates (`Check`).

@pub mod Level
@pub mod Grade
@pub mod Hir
@pub mod Core
@pub mod Value
@pub mod Tc
@pub mod Ctx
@pub mod Eval
@pub mod Unify
@pub mod Termination
@pub mod Positivity
@pub mod Usage
@pub mod Graph
@pub mod Cases
@pub mod Check

